cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite this formalization, please cite the specific archived version you checked, not
  the repository in general. Each release has its own version DOI; see the "Archival" section
  in README.md.
title: >-
  convex-uniform-honeycombs-lean: Lean 4 formalization of the pen-and-paper core of "The 28
  convex uniform honeycombs: a completeness theorem"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the human-checked mathematics around the finite
  certificates of the paper: the two-tier arithmetic (the irrationality of arctan sqrt 2 in
  degrees by Niven's theorem, and the split of every lattice angle equation into two integer
  equations), the closed-form tail lemmas A, B and E with the interleaving proved for every real
  q >= 4 and the tail corridors of the uncapped corona fixpoint, the separation constant of the
  species search as the exact value arctan sqrt 2 (the tetrahedral altitude), Identity I2, the
  forcing and rebasing arguments of the pattern section, and the constants, the box
  representative, the field identification and the box-rigidity step of the periodization section. The enumerations are
  exact certificates in the verification artifact and are not the target here. Every result is
  sorry-free and native_decide-free, depending at most on propext, Classical.choice and
  Quot.sound. The toolchain is pinned by lean-toolchain and lake-manifest.json, so lake exe
  cache get && lake build reproduces the checked build.
